---
title: Singaporean Curry Sauce
servings: 2
course: Main
locale: en_GB
difficulty: Medium
prep time: 15m
cook time: 40m
cuisine: Singaporean
tags:
- main-course
- savoury
- singaporean
---

Mix the @coconut milk{150%ml}, @sambal or chilli bean sauce{1%tbsp}, @light soy sauce{1%tbsp}, and @salt{0.5%tsp} ingredients in a jug to make the sauce.

Heat @vegetable oil{2%tbsp} in a saucepan to a medium heat. Fry the @onion{1}(finely diced) for 2 to ~{3%minutes}. Add the @ginger{0.%thumb}(peeled and finely chopped) and @garlic{2%cloves} and fry for ~{1%minute} or so.

Then add all the spices together (@star anise{2}, @cinnamon{1%stick}, and @curry powder{1.5%tbsp}), the @green chillies{3}(pierced with knife), and @potato{1}(cut into 5 cm chunks) in turn, frying for about ~{1%minute} after each addition.

Pour in a quarter of the sauce and bring to a vigorous boil. Add another quarter of the sauce and again bring to a boil, then repeat this process until all the sauce has been added. Bring to a boil once again.

Pour in the @chicken stock{300%ml}(cut into 3-4 cm lengths). Cook on a medium heat for ~{20%minutes}.

Add the @okra{200%g}. Cook for 5 to ~{10%minutes}.

> Serve with rice.